      "content": "Wait, what are those scores? I didn't ask for scores next to the comments. I think you might have misunderstood the \"score\" thing. \n\nAlso, this summary is still way too qualitative. It's just a list of the problems. For the infographic, the editors need to see specific technical data points—like estimated percentages of users affected or specific temperature/time metrics—to make it look like a real data report. \n\nCan you rewrite this as a single, professional technical brief? Make it much more data-heavy and precise so the density metric is higher, but again, please actually stick to what the users are saying. Don't just make up numbers if they aren't there, but try to find a way to represent these complaints with much more technical \"precision.\"",
